runs/

# ---- CARD GATE-0b (scrum/20260822/task_30): the ledger's own runs ----------
# `runs/` above has no leading slash, so git applies it at EVERY depth below
# this directory -- including `ledger/runs/`, which is not the bulky raw
# evidence the rule is aimed at but the four run files
# `ledger/runs.jsonl` POINTS AT by name. The ledger is tracked and its rows
# were unreadable in every clone:
# `test_barn_frontier_detour_v4.py::test_development_ledger_pins_full_report_hashes_without_requiring_reports`
# died on `ledger/runs/barn-v4-dev-reference-frontier-v3-20260803-run02.json`.
# A tracked index whose entries are ignored is a dangling pointer.
#
# MANIFEST: 4 files, 24 KB, under `ledger/runs/` only. `results/runs/`
# (4 files of raw candidate/reference dumps) stays ignored, which is what the
# rule above was written for.
!ledger/runs/
!ledger/runs/**
# ---- END CARD GATE-0b ------------------------------------------------------
